---
import Marketing from "../layouts/Marketing.astro";

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "");
const docs = `${base}/docs`;

const processes = [
  {
    num: "01",
    kicker: "Control plane",
    title: "The orchestrator",
    body: "The product surface and the only thing a person talks to. It owns sign-in and API keys, tasks and profiles, org secrets, the Slack, Linear, GitHub, and Google Cloud integrations, pull request review, automations, and the API the dashboard and CLI call. It is the deployment's login wall: the coordinator has no public address.",
    foot: "auth · tasks · integrations · api",
  },
  {
    num: "02",
    kicker: "Control plane",
    title: "The coordinator",
    body: "A stateless service in front of Postgres. It schedules sessions onto hosts, preferring the one that already holds a session's snapshot, evicts idle sessions, runs the pipeline that turns a pushed image into a base snapshot, stores and fans out every session event, and garbage-collects chunks nobody references. Run as many replicas as you like.",
    foot: "scheduler · eviction · events · gc",
  },
  {
    num: "03",
    kicker: "Every host",
    title: "The host agent",
    body: "One per machine that runs VMs. It dials the coordinator, registers its capacity, and runs the VMs; it owns the chunk cache on local NVMe, the NBD daemon that serves chunked disks, the page-fault handler that pages VM memory in lazily, and the egress proxy every VM's traffic goes through. Hosts never need an inbound port.",
    foot: "chunk cache · nbd · paging · egress",
  },
  {
    num: "04",
    kicker: "Every VM",
    title: "The in-guest daemon",
    body: "The first process after init inside every VM. It starts the harness, runs commands, moves files, and opens shells. It is not in your image: the host stages it in a bundle and the init shim copies it in at boot.",
    foot: "harness · exec · files · shells",
  },
];
---

<Marketing
  title="engrams architecture"
  description="Four processes, three external services, and the storage design that makes sessions cheap to pause, resume, and fork."
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="eyebrow label"><span class="pulse"></span>Architecture · Fig. A.1</div>
      <h1 class="display">Four processes and a blob store.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Two processes run in the control plane, one runs on every host, and one runs inside every
        VM. Postgres, a blob store, and an OCI registry are the only services around them.
      </p>
      <div class="codepane">
        <div class="bar"><span>Fig. A.1 · topology</span><span>dashboard → orchestrator → coordinator → hosts → blob store</span></div>
        <div class="arch-wrap">
          <div class="arch" data-fit="1248" aria-label="Topology: the dashboard, CLI, Slack, and webhooks reach the orchestrator; the orchestrator calls the coordinator, which owns Postgres and the OCI registry; host agents dial the coordinator and run microVMs; every host reads and writes the blob store.">
            <svg width="1248" height="620" viewBox="0 0 1248 620" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
              <defs>
                <marker id="arr" viewBox="0 0 8 8" refX="7" refY="4" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="8" orient="auto-start-reverse">
                  <path d="M0 0 L8 4 L0 8 Z" fill="currentColor" opacity=".7"></path>
                </marker>
              </defs>
              <path class="wire" d="M110 40 V64 H530 V40 M250 40 V64 M390 40 V64 M160 64 V116"></path>
              <path class="wire" d="M280 156 H358" marker-end="url(#arr)"></path>
              <path class="wire" d="M600 136 H678" marker-end="url(#arr)"></path>
              <path class="wire" d="M600 180 H678" marker-end="url(#arr)"></path>
              <path class="wire live" d="M190 340 V300 H830 V340 M510 300 V340 M480 300 V198" marker-end="url(#arr)"></path>
              <path class="wire" d="M190 490 V560 M510 490 V560 M830 490 V560"></path>
              <text x="496" y="290">hosts dial in · no inbound port</text>
            </svg>

            <div class="arch-entry" style="left:40px;top:0">
              {["dashboard", "CLI", "Slack", "webhooks"].map((e) => <span>{e}</span>)}
            </div>

            <div class="arch-group" style="left:16px;top:84px;width:888px;height:156px"><span>control plane · stateless pods</span></div>
            <div class="arch-node" style="left:40px;top:116px;width:240px;height:80px">
              <div class="kind"><span>process</span><span>login wall</span></div>
              <div class="name">orchestrator</div>
              <div class="meta">auth · tasks · integrations</div>
            </div>
            <div class="arch-node" style="left:360px;top:116px;width:240px;height:80px">
              <div class="kind"><span>process</span><span>n replicas</span></div>
              <div class="name">coordinator</div>
              <div class="meta">scheduling · eviction · gc</div>
            </div>
            <div class="arch-node service" style="left:680px;top:100px;width:200px;height:52px">
              <div class="kind"><span>service</span></div>
              <div class="name">Postgres</div>
            </div>
            <div class="arch-node service" style="left:680px;top:164px;width:200px;height:52px">
              <div class="kind"><span>service</span></div>
              <div class="name">OCI registry</div>
            </div>

            <div class="arch-key" style="left:1040px;top:84px;width:208px;height:156px">
              <div class="k">key</div>
              <div><i class="process"></i>a process engrams ships</div>
              <div><i class="service"></i>a service you run</div>
              <div><i class="vm"></i>one session's microVM</div>
              <div><i class="wire"></i>hosts dial out</div>
            </div>

            <div class="arch-group" style="left:16px;top:316px;width:1000px;height:204px"><span>host fleet · linux + kvm</span></div>
            {[0, 1].map((i) => (
              <div class="arch-node host" style={`left:${40 + i * 320}px;top:340px;width:300px;height:150px`}>
                <div class="kind"><span>process · per machine</span><span>kvm · nvme</span></div>
                <div class="name">host agent</div>
                <div class="meta">chunk cache · nbd · lazy paging · egress proxy</div>
                <div class="vms">
                  <div class="vm"><b>microVM</b><span>harness · daemon</span></div>
                  <div class="vm"><b>microVM</b><span>harness · daemon</span></div>
                </div>
              </div>
            ))}
            <div class="arch-node host ghost" style="left:680px;top:340px;width:300px;height:150px">
              <div class="kind"><span>process · per machine</span></div>
              <div class="name">host agent</div>
              <div class="meta">as many as the fleet needs</div>
              <div class="vms">
                <div class="vm"><b>…</b><span></span></div>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="arch-node service wide" style="left:40px;top:560px;width:960px;height:56px">
              <div class="kind"><span>service</span><span>gcs · s3 · local</span></div>
              <div class="name">blob store <em>image chunks · memory chunks · snapshots</em></div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sec">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head"><span class="sec-badge">Sec. 1</span><span>The processes</span><span class="sec-rule"></span></div>
      <div class="modules">
        {processes.map((p) => (
          <div class="hud">
            <div class="rail"></div>
            <div class="kicker"><span>{p.kicker}</span><i></i></div>
            <div class="num">{p.num}</div>
            <h2 class="display">{p.title}</h2>
            <p>{p.body}</p>
            <div class="foot">{p.foot}</div>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sec">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head"><span class="sec-badge">Sec. 2</span><span>Storage</span><span class="sec-rule"></span></div>
      <div class="sec-intro">
        <h2 class="display md">Storage is what makes the rest cheap.</h2>
        <div class="prose">
          <p>
            Disk and memory state live as immutable chunks named by the hash of their content, with
            versioned manifests pointing at them. An image's base snapshot is written once and shared
            by every session of that image; a session's manifest gains entries only for the chunks it
            wrote. That gives three levels of copy-on-write for free: on disk, in memory through the
            hardware's memory management unit, and on fork, which is a manifest copy of a few
            kilobytes.
          </p>
          <p>
            A VM reads its disk through an NBD device served from its manifest and pages memory in
            lazily from chunks, with the chunks a session touched in its first seconds prefaulted
            before the CPUs start. A snapshot writes only the delta and destroys the VM. Restoring on
            a different host fetches the delta.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="btn primary" href={`${docs}/concepts/architecture/`}>Architecture in the docs</a>
        <a class="btn ghost" href={`${docs}/concepts/storage-and-snapshots/`}>Storage and snapshots</a>
        <a class="btn ghost" href={`${docs}/concepts/sandbox-backends/`}>Sandbox backends</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <div style="height:128px"></div>
</Marketing>

<script>
  import "../scripts/fit";
</script>
